{
  "id": "attention-network-test",
  "term": "Attention Network Test",
  "definition": "The Attention Network Test is a task paradigm used to measure how efficiently key attention systems work, especially alerting, orienting, and executive control. It typically uses cues and target–flanker trials to separate these aspects of attention by comparing performance under different cueing and conflict conditions.",
