      "reasons": [
        "The field is not supported: the packet describes the Attention Network Test as a cognitive task paradigm / assessment tool, not a diagnosis term.",
        "The definition is generally supported on the three attention networks and cue/flanker structure, but it overstates “how efficiently key attention systems work” as a broad characterization rather than the packet’s narrower claim about assessing the efficiency of attentional subsystems and experimentally dissociating them.",
        "The phrase “target–flanker trials” is defensible, but the packet frames the task specifically as a cued-flanker task; the definition should not imply a generic or standardized trial structure beyond what is stated in the source."
